WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:07.760
Payment pay-77 must end up captured or voided, never both.

2
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.243
P1 wants capture.

3
00:00:09.243 --> 00:00:10.464
P2 wants void.

4
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.048
Three nodes, called acceptors, decide.

5
00:00:13.048 --> 00:00:20.003
Each one keeps two notes on disk: the highest ballot number it has promised, and the last proposal it accepted.

6
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.647
A value is chosen once a majority, two of the three, accept it under the same ballot.

7
00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:28.639
P1 picks ballot 1.1: round 1, from P1.

8
00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:31.192
It sends prepare to every acceptor.

9
00:00:31.192 --> 00:00:36.809
It means: promise to ignore anything lower, and tell me what you've accepted.

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.450
A1 and A2 promise.

11
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.867
Neither has accepted anything.

12
00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:45.297
Two promises are a majority, so P1 doesn't wait for A3.

13
00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:49.005
No value came back, so P1 may use its own.

14
00:00:49.005 --> 00:00:51.449
It sends accept 1.1, capture.

15
00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:53.134
A1 and A2 accept it.

16
00:00:53.134 --> 00:00:55.072
The copy to A3 is lost.

17
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.854
Capture is now chosen.

18
00:00:56.854 --> 00:01:01.741
Then P1 crashes before any reply reaches it, so nobody knows yet.

19
00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:04.921
P2 hears nothing, and its timer fires.

20
00:01:04.921 --> 00:01:08.773
It picks a higher ballot, 2.2, and sends prepare.

21
00:01:08.773 --> 00:01:11.681
A1 is slow, so only A2 and A3 answer.

22
00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:14.877
A3 promises, with nothing to report.

23
00:01:14.877 --> 00:01:21.565
A2 raises its promise to 2.2, and reports what it accepted: ballot 1.1, capture.

24
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:22.918
Here is the rule.

25
00:01:22.918 --> 00:01:27.318
P2 must propose the value from the highest ballot it heard about.

26
00:01:27.318 --> 00:01:29.552
That's capture, not its own void.

27
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.164
It sends accept 2.2, capture.

28
00:01:32.164 --> 00:01:36.668
A2 and A3 accept, and P2 learns the outcome: capture.

29
00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:38.151
It had to be capture.

30
00:01:38.151 --> 00:01:40.965
Any two majorities of three share an acceptor.

31
00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:45.676
Here that's A2, which carried the value from the first round into the second.

32
00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:49.912
So once a value is chosen, every later ballot proposes it again.

33
00:01:49.912 --> 00:01:53.389
A crash can delay the decision, but it can't change it.
